"To determine the number of lattice points on the line \\( y = -2x + 18 \\) where \\( x \\geq 0 \\) and \\( y \\geq 0 \\), we need to find the integer solutions \\((x, y)\\) that satisfy the equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation as:\n\\[ y = -2x + 18 \\]\n\nSince \\( x \\geq 0 \\) and \\( y \\geq 0 \\), we substitute \\( x = 0 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ y = -2(0) + 18 = 18 \\]\n\nThus, the lattice point is:\n\\[ (0, 18) \\]\n\nThis is the only lattice point on the line \\( y = -2x + 18 \\) where \\( x \\geq 0 \\) and \\( y \\geq 0 \\).\n\nTherefore, the number of lattice points on the line is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1} \\]"
