"We know that the number of games played in a round-robin tournament with $n$ teams is given by the formula $\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$. We are given that the number of games played is 55, so we can set up the equation:\n\n$$\\frac{n(n-1)}{2} = 55$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n$$n(n-1) = 110$$\n\nWe can solve this quadratic equation by factoring:\n\n$$n^2 - n - 110 = 0$$\n\n$$(n-11)(n+10) = 0$$\n\nSo, $n = 11$ or $n = -10$. Since the number of teams cannot be negative, we have $n = 11$.\n\nTherefore, the number of teams in the round-robin tournament is $\\boxed{11}$."
