"Let \\( r \\) be the number of regular packs and \\( s \\) be the number of super packs. We have two equations:\n\n1. \\( r + s = 32 \\)\n2. \\( 4r + 6s = 166 \\)\n\nFirst, simplify the second equation by dividing everything by 2:\n\\[ 2r + 3s = 83 \\]\n\nNow we have the system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nr + s = 32 \\\\\n2r + 3s = 83\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(2r + 3s) - (r + s) = 83 - 32\n\\]\n\\[\ns = 51\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( s = 51 \\) back into the first equation:\n\\[\nr + 51 = 32\n\\]\n\\[\nr = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of regular packs sent is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
