"The vertex of the parabola described by the equation $y=-2x^2-12x-15$ is $(m,n)$. To find the vertex, we can complete the square.\n\nFirst, we factor out the coefficient of $x^2$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$y=-2(x^2+6x)-15$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$x^2+6x=(x+3)^2-9$$\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n$$y=-2((x+3)^2-9)-15$$\n\n$$y=-2(x+3)^2+18-15$$\n\n$$y=-2(x+3)^2+3$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is $(-3,3)$.\n\nSo, $m+n=-3+3=\\boxed{0}$."
